# SRG-APP-000108-WSR-000166  -  CAT II
# The web server must use a logging mechanism that is configured to alert
# the ISSO and SA in the event of a processing failure.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000108-WSR-000166
group:           V-206366
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000139
control_rev5:    AU-5

contribution:    Splunk's health reporter watches its own features, including the indexing
                 and queue features that signal a log processing failure, and fires the
                 alert actions named in health.conf when a feature holds at the threshold
                 color; alert_actions.conf [email] configures the delivery channel. A
                 scheduled saved search with action.email, action.email.to and an
                 alert_condition is the product's second route to the same notification.

governs:         alert_actions.conf - What Splunk does when an alert fires, such as sending email or calling a
                 webhook.
governs:         health.conf - Thresholds for Splunk reporting on its own health.

check:           health.conf [health_reporter] alert.disabled equals 0
check:           health.conf [health_reporter] alert.actions non_empty
check:           alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver not_equals localhost
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       alert_actions.conf [email] email present -> alert_actions.conf [email] mailserver not_equals localhost
vendor:          alert_actions.conf [email] email https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.3-configuration-file-reference/alert_actions.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The SMTP relay that carries the notification, and the ISSO and SA
                 addresses it is sent to, are organization-defined; alert_actions.conf
                 holds the mail server and sender but the recipients are the organization's
                 to supply, so the criterion tests only that the product can express them.
external:        A processing failure that stops splunkd outright - a full filesystem, a
                 terminated process - cannot be alerted on by the application itself and is
                 reported by the operating system's own monitoring.
external:        The ISSO and SA role assignments are organizational designations.

citation:        SRG-APP-000108-WSR-000166 check text; health.conf.spec:32
                 ([health_reporter]), :88-91 (alert.disabled = [0|1], Default: 0), :93-94
                 (alert.actions = <string>), :96-99 (alert.min_duration_sec = <integer>,
                 Default: 60), :101-103 (alert.threshold_color = [yellow|red], Default:
                 red), :105-110 (alert.suppress_period = <integer>[m|s|h|d], Default: 10m);
                 alert_actions.conf.spec:157-162 ([email]); savedsearches.conf.spec:73-77
                 (enableSched = [0 | 1], Default: 0), :270-274 (alert_condition = <search
                 string>), :300-306 (action.email = <boolean>, Default: false;
                 action.email.to = <email list>, REQUIRED)
finding:         health.conf disables the health reporter's alerting (alert.disabled = 1),
                 names no alert actions, or has no configured email action, so Splunk
                 Enterprise raises no alert to the ISSO and SA when a log processing
                 failure occurs.
